{
  "pdf_page": 58,
  "book_page": 28,
  "verified_by": "claude-fable-5-1",
  "verified_on": "2026-09-04",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 0,
      "root": "Ap 2",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "modern_form": "PIE *h₁ep- 'to take, seize, reach' (Pokorny '1. ap- (richtiger əp-) : ep- \"fassen, nehmen, erreichen\"', IEW 50-51; Watkins/AHD ap-¹ 'To take, reach'; LIV *h₁ep-)",
      "note": "Root, language label and gloss are all correct: Pokorny's entry begins at the foot of p.50 (exactly Nourai's POK:50) and runs onto p.51, with Av. apayeiti, Skt. āpnóti, Lat. apiscor/apere/aptus/apex/cōpula and Hitt. epmi — i.e. precisely the two branches Nourai draws. The only correction is that the modern reconstruction has an initial laryngeal (*h₁ep-), which is why Hittite has e-ep-zi and Latin co-ēpī shows e-vocalism. Nourai's numbering 'Ap 2' distinguishes this root from 'Ap 1' = *h₂ep- 'water' (Pokorny 2. āp- p.51), which is the right distinction. The weak point of the page is not the root but the Iranian branch: Cheung 2007 removes MP abām 'loan' from this root altogether (see node 2).",
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/h₁ep-",
        "https://www.etymonline.com/word/apt"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {"ref": "POK:50", "status": "supports", "note": "POK_01.txt ff-page 59-60 (printed 50-51, the entry straddles the page break): '1. ap- (richtiger əp-) : ep- \"fassen, nehmen, erreichen\". Ai. āpnóti \"erreicht, erlangt\" ... av. apayeiti \"erreicht\" ... lat. apiscor \"fasse, erreiche\", adipiscor \"erlange\", coepi ... Zusammenhang mit lat. *apiō, *apere \"comprehendere vinculo\" ... aptus \"verknüpft\", cōpula (co-apula) \"Band\" ... lat. apex, -icis \"Spitze\" ... gehört vielleicht zu *apiō ... hitt. e-ip-mi \"nehme\". WP. I 45 f.' — the cited page is exactly Nourai's root and his Latin node."}
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Avestan / Old Persian",
          "words": "ap 1, af, ab : to receive ; apayeiti : received ; abi-âp, abi-âf : to detain",
          "verdict": "plausible",
          "derivation": "Avestan ap- 'to reach, attain' (present stem apaiia-, 3sg. apaiieiti Yt 10.21, 14.20, 17.19; 1sg. apaiiemi Yt 5.42, 15.43; perf. āpa; OAv. 1pl. opt. apaema Y 41.2) is the regular Iranian continuant of PIE *h₁ep-: *h₁p-eie- > Ir. *apaya-, with intervocalic *p preserved in Avestan. Nourai's 'af, ab' are not Avestan or Old Persian forms at all but retrojections of the later Iranian outcomes, where Old Iranian *p in postvocalic position lenites through *β to Middle/New Persian f (before a consonant / word-finally) and b/w (before a vowel): hence MP ayāft ~ ayāb-, NP yāft ~ yāb-. Old Persian has no attested reflex of this root (Kent's lexicon has none), so the label 'Avestan / Old Persian' overstates the evidence. The compound is Av. aiβi-/avi-ap- (Nyberg: 'ay- probably < abi-, cf Av. avi-ap-'; Cheung: '(+ *abi-) to obtain, find'), and its meaning is 'to obtain, reach, find' — NOT 'to detain'. The scan of p.28 does print 'to detain', so this is Nourai's own slip (probably for 'to obtain'), not a transcription error in the JSON.",
          "sources": [
            "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/h₁ep-",
            "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/یافتن"
          ],
          "ref_check": [
            {"ref": "POK:50", "status": "supports", "note": "POK_01.txt ff-page 59 (printed 50): 'Ai. āpnóti \"erreicht, erlangt\" ... av. apayeiti \"erreicht\", 3. Pl. apənte aus *āpuantai' — the Avestan form and gloss are exactly as charted."},
            {"ref": "SNS:14", "status": "not_found", "note": "SNS_pages.txt: the Šāyast nē Šāyast glossary OCR is very poor. The a-/ab- stretch of the glossary is ff-leaf 29 (≈ printed p.14) and there I can read 'abdum/afdum ... (HuIVb. 80-81) *apatəma, apama' and abartar/abē-mōzag/aburnāy/afrīn/agar, but no legible ap-/apām entry. grep for 'apam|ayaf|ayab|awam' across ff-leaves 26-33 returns only that *apatəma line."},
            {"ref": "FFD:82", "status": "supports", "note": "FFD_pages.txt [pdf page 87] = printed p.82, s.v. یافتن: 'یافت < فارسی میانه ayāft < ایرانی باستان *abi-āp-ta-… ای پیشوند فعلی است. ریشهٔ āp به معنی «به دست آوردن» است.' — Abolghasemi's root is āp 'to obtain', with abi- as the preverb, i.e. Nourai's 'abi-âp' but glossed 'to obtain', not 'to detain'."}
          ],
          "consulted": [
            {"src": "BRT", "where": "s.v. ap-, col. ~74 (BRT.txt lines 3478-3479)", "stance": "supports", "note": "Bartholomae gives the paradigm apayeiti with senses '1) einholen, nachkommen 2) gelangen zu —, teilhaftig werden 3) treffen (vom Geschoss) 4) (einem Gebot) nachkommen', citing Yt 10.21, Yt 14.20, Y 41.2 — the root and the form apayeiti are exactly as charted."},
            {"src": "CHEUNG", "where": "pp. 161-162 s.v. *Hap/f", "stance": "supports", "note": "'*Hap/f \"to reach, attain\" — *AVESTAN: ap- \"to reach, attain\" || (+ *abi-) \"to obtain, find\" || (+ *pati-) \"to reach to\" || (+ *pari-) \"to reach, attain\"'; forms listed: YAv. apaiiemi, apaiieiti, apaiieinti, OAv. apaema, perf. āpa. Confirms the root and gives 'to obtain, find' for the abi- compound."},
            {"src": "WLD", "where": "Bd. I p. 45 (WLD_Bd1 djvu lines 3112-3140)", "stance": "supports", "note": "'1. ap- \"erreichen\". Ai. āpnóti \"erreicht, erlangt\" ... av. apayeiti \"erreicht\". Lat. apiscor \"fasse, erreiche\", adipiscor \"erlange\", coepi ...' — Walde-Pokorny I 45 f. is the source Pokorny 50 refers to."},
            {"src": "AHD", "where": "Watkins appendix s.v. ap-¹", "stance": "supports", "note": "'ap-¹. To take, reach. 1. Latin apere, to attach, join, tie to: APT, (APTITUDE), ATTITUDE; (INEPT). 2. Latin apisci, to attain: ADEPT. 3. Latin apex ... 4. Prefixed form *co-ap- ... cōpula ... [Pok. 1. ap- 50.]'"},
            {"src": "KNT", "where": "Old Persian lexicon", "stance": "silent", "note": "Kent has no Old Persian verb ap-/āp- 'to reach'; the only Bāx-/ap- material in the lexicon is Bāxtriš and the preposition apa-. So the 'Old Persian' half of the language label is unsupported."}
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "lang": "Pahlavi",
          "words": "apâm, avâm : loan, something received.",
          "verdict": "disputed",
          "derivation": "Book Pahlavi ʾpʾm /abām/ 'loan, debt' is well attested (MacKenzie p.4; Nyberg II 22; Parthian ʾbʾmyh 'loan'). Nourai, following Nyberg and Mo'in, analyses it as Old Iranian *(ā-)apamna-, a middle participle of ap- 'to reach, obtain' — literally 'that which the lender has to obtain back', hence his gloss 'something received'. Cheung's Etymological Dictionary of the Iranian Verb (2007) rejects this: he files abām under the root *Hmai¹ 'to (ex)change' (< PIE *h₂mei-, Pok. 710, LIV 426) as a *apa- compound, comparing Sanskrit apa-mitya- 'something borrowed, debt' (Kāṭhaka+) from may- 'to exchange', Parth. ʾbʾmyh, Sogd. pʾmytʾy/pʾmytk 'loan' and Bactrian βαμδοιγο 'loan', and states in as many words that 'the etymology and reconstruction given by Nyberg 1974: 22a … from partic. med. *(ā-)apamna-, is less convincing'. The Sanskrit parallel apamitya- is decisive for Cheung because it gives a perfect semantic and morphological match ('borrowing' = 'exchanging away'), whereas *apamna- would be a unique formation. The modern standard therefore prefers a different origin, so the arrow root→apām is disputed; note that the two etymologies share the preverb *apa- and differ only in the verbal root (*Hap 'reach' vs *Hmai 'exchange').",
          "sources": [
            "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/وام"
